 The given expression is equivalent to $\boxed{\textbf{(D)}\ \tan \frac{x}{2}}$ because \begin{align*} \frac{1 + \sin x - \cos x}{1 + \sin x + \cos x} &= \frac{\left(1 + \sin x - \cos x\right)\left(1 + \sin x - \cos x\right)}{\left(1 + \sin x + \cos x\right)\left(1 + \sin x - \cos x\right)} 
&= \frac{\left(1 + \sin x\right)^2 - \cos^2 x}{\left(1 + \sin x\right)^2 - \cos^2 x} 
&= \frac{1 + 2\sin x + \sin^2 x - \cos^2 x}{1 + 2\sin x + \sin^2 x - \cos^2 x}
&= \frac{2\sin^2 x + 2\sin x}{2\sin^2 x + 2\sin x} = \tan \frac{x}{2}. \end{align*>think 

